					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs  accordion"  aria-hidden="False.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" >
						<li class="" role="presentation">	<a href="#tabcf71331b-a8c3-4e88-a4a4-eac8f185ef95_9" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrowcf71331b-a8c3-4e88-a4a4-eac8f185ef95_9" role="button" aria-controls="tabcf71331b-a8c3-4e88-a4a4-eac8f185ef95_9" aria-expanded="false" ><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="9" data-tabname="Judicial Offices" contenteditable="false">Judicial Offices</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel " style="display: none;" id="tabcf71331b-a8c3-4e88-a4a4-eac8f185ef95_9" role="region" aria-labelledby="tabBtncf71331b-a8c3-4e88-a4a4-eac8f185ef95_9" >

<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor126168d3-1bd2-4096-aec6-bba88f4268d4" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <h2 class="subhead1" id="isPasted"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">United States Supreme Court Justices</span></h2><p><br><span style="font-size: 18px;">Phone: 202-479-3211&nbsp;<br><a href="https://www.supremecourt.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-size: 18px;" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">U.S. Supreme Court Website</a></span><br><br></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">The Members of the Supreme Court are appointed by the President, subject to the approval of the Senate. To ensure an independent Judiciary and to protect judges from partisan pressures, the Constitution provides that judges serve during &quot;Good Behavior&quot;, which has generally meant justices serve for life terms. To further assure their independence, the Constitution provides that judges&apos; salaries may not be diminished while they are in office. The Constitution of the United States of America provides that there shall be nine justices. For a complete biography of justices, visit the <a href="https://www.supremecourt.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-size: 18px;" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">U.S Supreme Court Website</a>.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">Justices are non-partisan officeholders.</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Samuel Anthony Alito, Jr.</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Ketanji Brown Jackson</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Amy Coney Barrett</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Elena Kagan</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Brett M. Kavanaugh</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>John Glover Roberts Jr (Chief Justice)</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Sonia Maria Sotomayor</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Clarence Thomas</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Neil Gorsuch</strong><br><br></span></p><h2 class="subhead1"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">Florida Supreme Court Justices</span></h2><p><br><span style="font-size: 18px;">Supreme Court of Florida<br>500 South Duval St<br>Tallahassee, FL 32399-1925<br>Phone: 850-488-0125 (Office of the Clerk)<br><a href="https://www.supremecourt.flcourts.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-size: 18px;" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Florida Supreme Court Website</a></span><br><br></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">The term for a Florida Supreme Court Justice is six years upon successful &quot;Merit Retention&quot;. Justices are non-partisan officeholders.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">Whenever a vacancy occurs in a judicial office to which election for retention applies, the governor shall fill the vacancy by appointing for a term ending on the first Tuesday after the first Monday in January of the year following the next general election occurring at least one year after the date of appointment. An election will then be held to fill that judicial office for the term of the office, beginning at the end of the appointed term.</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><br></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>John D. Couriel</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Renatha Francis</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Jamie Grosshans</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Jorge Labarga</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Carlos Mu&ntilde;iz (Chief Justice)</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Meredith Sasso</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Adam S. Tanenbaum</strong><br><br></span></p><h2 class="subhead1"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">Sixth District Court of Appeal Judges</span></h2><p><br><span style="font-size: 18px;"><a href="https://www.6dca.flcourts.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-size: 18px;" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Sixth District Court of Appeal Website</a></span><br><br></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">The Sixth District Court of Appeals includes the 9th, 10th, and 20th Judicial Circuits.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">The term for a Florida Appellate Court Judge is six years upon successful &quot;Merit Retention&quot;. Judges are non-partisan officeholders.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">Whenever a vacancy occurs in a judicial office to which election for retention applies, the governor shall fill the vacancy by appointing for a term ending on the first Tuesday after the first Monday in January of the year following the next general election occurring at least one year after the date of appointment. An election will then be held to fill that judicial office for the term of the office, beginning at the end of the appointed term.</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Paetra Brownlee</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Roger Gannam</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Rachel Kamoutsas</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Joshua Mize</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Mary Alice Nardella</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Joshua Pratt</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Jared E. Smith</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>John K. Stargel</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Dan Traver (Chief Judge)</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Keith F. White</strong></span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Carrie Ann Wozniak</strong><br><br></span></p><h2 class="subhead1"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">County Court Judges</span></h2><p><br><span style="font-size: 18px;">Phone: 239-533-1700<br><a href="http://www.ca.cjis20.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-size: 18px;" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Lee County Court Website</a></span><br><br></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">The term for an elected Lee County Court Judge is six years. Judges are non-partisan officeholders.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">The governor shall fill each vacancy on a circuit court or on a county court, where the judges are elected by a majority vote of the electors, by appointing for a term ending on the first Tuesday after the first Monday in January of the year following the next primary and general election occurring at least one year after the date of appointment. An election will then be held to fill that judicial office for the term of the office, beginning at the end of the appointed term.</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Zachary Gill</strong><br>County Judge Group 1</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Nicole Mirra</strong><br>County Judge Group 2</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Devin George</strong><br>County Judge Group 3</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Lindsay Scott Garza</strong><br>County Judge Group 4</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Michael Colombo</strong><br>County Judge Group 5</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Josephine Gagliardi</strong><br>County Judge Group 6</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Maria E Gonzalez</strong><br>County Judge Group 7</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Tara Pascotto Paluck</strong><br>County Judge Group 8</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Kristan Burns</strong><br>County Judge Group 9<br><br></span></p><h2 class="subhead1"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">Twentieth Judicial Circuit Judges</span></h2><p><br><span style="font-size: 18px;">Phone: 239-533-1700<br><a href="http://www.ca.cjis20.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-size: 18px;" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Twentieth Judicial Circuit Court Website</a></span><br><br></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">The Twentieth Judicial Circuit includes Charlotte, Collier, Glades, Hendry, and Lee Counties.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">The term for a Florida Circuit Court Judge is six years upon successful &quot;Merit Retention&quot;. Judges are non-partisan officeholders.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">The governor shall fill each vacancy on a circuit court or on a county court, where the judges are elected by a majority vote of the electors, by appointing for a term ending on the first Tuesday after the first Monday in January of the year following the next primary and general election occurring at least one year after the date of appointment. An election will then be held to fill that judicial office for the term of the office, beginning at the end of the appointed term.</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Carolyn Swift</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 1</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Frank Porter (Chief Judge)</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 2</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Kimberly Bocelli</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 3</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Shannon McFee</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 4</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Geoffrey Gentile</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 5</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Tracey L. Redd</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 6</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>James R. Shenko</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 7</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>John McGowan</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 8</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Trent Reichling</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 9</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Nick Thompson</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 10</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Andrew Marcus</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 11</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Russell Kirshy</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 12</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Ramiro Manalich</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 13</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Bruce Kyle</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 14</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Alane C. Laboda</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 15</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Amy Hawthorne</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 16</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Christopher H. Brown</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 17</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Joe Foster</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 18</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>James Stewart</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 19</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Vacant</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 20</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Kyle Cohen</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 21</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Lauren L. Brodie</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 22</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Rachael Loukonen</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 23</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Robert Branning</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 24</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Michael T. McHugh</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 25</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Lisa Porter</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 26</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Amanda Levy-Reis</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 27</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>James Chandler</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 28</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Gilberto Perez</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 29</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Elisabeth Adams</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 30</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Keith R. Kyle</strong><br>Circuit Judge Group 31</span></p><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Darrell R. Hill</strong></span><br><span style="font-size: 18px;">Circuit Judge Group 32</span></p>
    </div>

