        <h2 class="subhead1"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">City of Bonita Springs</span></h2><p id="isPasted"><span style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;"><br></span><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">9101 Bonita Beach RD<br>Bonita Springs, FL &nbsp;34135<br>239-949-6262</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><a data-fr-linked="true" href="http://www.cityofbonitasprings.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">City of Bonita Springs Website</a></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">A vacancy shall be filled in accordance with the municipal charter. Municipal officers are non-partisan officeholders.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">4-Year Term</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Mayor</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Mike Gibson</strong><br>Next Election: 2028</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Council District 1</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Jamie Bogacz</strong><br>Next Election: 2026</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Council District 2</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Jesse Purdon</strong><br>Next Election: 2028</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Council District 3</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Laura E. Carr</strong><br>Next Election: 2026 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Council District 4</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Chris Corrie</strong><br>Next Election: 2028</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Council District 5</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Nigel Patrick Fullick</strong><br>Next Election: 2026 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Council District 6</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Jim Fitzpatrick</strong><br>Next Election: 2028&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><br></span></p><h2 class="subhead1" aria-level="2"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">City of Cape Coral</span></h2><p><span style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;"><br></span><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">1015 Cultural Parkway<br>Cape Coral, FL 33990<br>239-574-0417</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><a data-fr-linked="true" href="https://www.capecoral.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">City of Cape Coral Website</a></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">01-14-19 Ordinance 81-18 issued by the City of Cape Coral changes the Municipal Election schedule to even years beginning 2020.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">A vacancy shall be filled in accordance with the municipal charter. &nbsp;Municipal officers are non-partisan officeholders.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">4-Year Term</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Mayor</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>John Gunter</strong><br>Next Election: 2026</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Council District 1</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Bill&nbsp;</strong><strong>Steinke</strong><br>Next Election: 2026</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Council District 2</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Laurie&nbsp;</strong><strong>Lehmann</strong><br>Next Election: 2028</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Council District 3</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Derrick&nbsp;</strong><strong>Donnell</strong><br>Next Election: 2028</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Council District 4</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Jennifer&nbsp;</strong><strong>Nelson</strong><br>Next Election: 2026</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Council District 5</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Joseph&nbsp;</strong><strong>Kilraine</strong><br>Next Election: 2028 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Council District 6</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Keith Long</strong><br>Next Election: 2026</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Council District 7</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Rachel Kaduk</strong><br>Next Election: 2028</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><br></span></p><h2 class="subhead1" aria-level="2"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">City of Fort Myers</span></h2><p><span style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;"><br></span><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">2200 Second St<br>Fort Myers, FL 33901</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">239-321-7020 (Mayor&apos;s Office)<br>239-321-7035 (City Clerk&apos;s Office)</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><a data-fr-linked="true" href="http://cityftmyers.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">City of Fort Myers Website</a></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">The City of Fort Myers decided to move its Primary and General Elections to even-numbered years beginning in 2020.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">A vacancy shall be filled in accordance with the municipal charter. Municipal officers are non-partisan officeholders.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">4-Year Term</span><span style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;"><br></span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Mayor</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Kevin Anderson</strong><br>Next Election: 2026</span></p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">City Ward 1</span></h3><p style="margin-left: 20px;"